  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 109 PM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nThursday through Saturday, ridging is forecast to build \nnorthward into southern Canada as high pressure at the surface \nmoves into the Mid Atlantic states. As the surface high moves \noff shore Friday into Saturday, the pressure gradient across \nthe Midwest will gradually tighten leading to potentially \nbreezy conditions Friday into Saturday. High temperatures will \ngradually modify each day with highs in the 70s. Cloud cover \nmay also increase Friday into Saturday as a storm system \ndevelops to our west.\n\nSunday through Monday, a 500 mb shortwave trough is forecast to\ndig into the Upper Midwest. This pushes a cold front \nsoutheastward across the area early next week. This front will \ngradually become parallel to the flow as it moves southeastward\nearly next week causing it to stall out in southern Iowa or \nnorthern Missouri. The NBM has 15 to 25% chance POPs Sunday \nnight through Monday across the area. High temperatures on \nSunday remain in the lower to mid 70s ahead of the front with \ntemperatures falling into the 60s on Monday behind the front.\nDespite cooler high temperatures, these remain above normal for\nthe last week of October when high temperatures are normally in\nthe mid to upper 50s. Rainfall amounts will be light with less \nthan a tenth of an inch for rainfall.",
